    description: "scripts/ci-debug 'logs woodpecker' crashes instead of printing the failed\njob log: 'TypeError: NoneType object is not iterable' followed by\n'Woodpecker log fetch failed (HTTP 200)'. Observed live 2026-08-01 while\ndiagnosing PR #144's errored woodpecker run — the one situation the\nsubcommand exists for. An HTTP 200 whose body parses to None (empty JSON,\nor a shape change in the log endpoint) is treated as iterable. Effect: the\noperator is blind exactly when CI is failing; auto-pr's own '(could not\nretrieve log automatically)' fallback traces to the same fetch. NOTE:\nci-debug is a GOVERNANCE file — human approval workflow required for the\nfix."  # 918d
    fields: {}  # 918d
