  message: "CLOSED done — PR #147, dev ae50ba3a43 (2026-08-01).\n\nFIX: the Woodpecker log parse now checks isinstance(entries, list) before\nsorting; a 200-with-null (or error-envelope object) body is diagnosed as\n\"returned NoneType, not a log-entry list (an error response with a 200\ncode)\" and degrades to the documented credential-guidance fallback.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (the item own filed symptom, re-run as tests): the\nnew TestWoodpeckerLogBodyShapes suite drives the REAL _github_fetch_job_log\nend-to-end through the harness fake curl — upgraded to emulate the\nno-dash-o + -w http_code shape the Woodpecker calls use, which is WHY this\npath had no coverage before — and asserts: null body -> RC=1, no\nTraceback, shape named; error-envelope object -> same; a real entry list\nstill base64-decodes in line order (happy path pinned through the same\nharness). 21/21 green across the forge-backend and ci-debug suites."  # 66f9
